data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"content\": \"# Reply: d002 — greet, tested\\n\\n## What I did\\n\\nImplemented all three deliverables in `~/subject` on branch\\n`cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>`:\\n\\n1. `src/greet.py` — defines `greet(name)` returning `\\\"Hello, \\\" + name + \\\"!\\\"`.\\n   `greet(\\\"World\\\")` → `\\\"Hello, World!\\\"`; `greet(\\\"\\\")` → `\\\"Hello, !\\\"`.\\n2. `tests/test_greet.py` — a `unittest` module with two cases:\\n   - `test_normal_name`: `greet(\\\"World\\\")` → `\\\"Hello, World!\\\"`\\n   - `test_empty_string`: `greet(\\\"\\\")` → `\\\"Hello, !\\\"`\\n   The test inserts `\u003crepo\u003e/src` into `sys.path` (relative to the test file) so\\n   `from greet import greet` works when run from the repository root.\\n3. Ran `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` from the repository root.\\n\\n## Test result (exact output)\\n\\n```\\n$ python3 -m unittest discover -s tests\\n..\\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\\nRan 2 tests in 0.000s\\n\\nOK\\n```\\n\\nExit status: **0**.\\n\\n## Commit\\n\\n- `3330d4e Implement greet module with unittest tests (d002)` — adds\\n  `src/greet.py` and `tests/test_greet.py` (2 files, 21 insertions) on top of\\n  base `96a01e4`.\\n\\nEverything requested is committed on my own branch; the working tree is clean.\\n\", \"filePath\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/d002-reply.md\"}","name":"write"},"id":"write_10","index":0,"type":"function"}]},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1788397682,"id":"chatcmpl-cbfd42b8ee9f4a96bc05de34f25e3e7d","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k3","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

